One directory, named once, so the ROM scan finds it

`GetAppBundlePath` and `GetAppDirectoryPath` both fall through to `"."` here: none
of the platform branches match, and `NON_PORTABLE` is not set. That answer is not
wrong - a payload's one directory really is where it is running from - but it is
the worst spelling of it. Every path built from it carries a `.` component through
`std::filesystem`, and those reach the kernel, which resolves nothing. `/app0/./
soh.o2r` is how that looked the first time: the archive sitting there, reported
missing.

`OOPS_POSIX_HOME` is the build's name for the mount, and `common/posix/posix.c`
resolves relative paths against the same place, so naming it here keeps the two in
step instead of leaving `.` to be undone further down.

Saying it twice has one consequence worth handling. `OTRGlobals` scans the bundle
path and then the app directory looking for a ROM to convert, and those are now
visibly the same directory - so a single ROM was listed twice and offered for
conversion a second time the moment the first conversion finished. `GetRoms` keeps
a set. Every caller wants one; on the platforms where the two paths differ this
changes nothing.

diff --git a/libultraship/src/ship/Context.cpp b/libultraship/src/ship/Context.cpp
index 88ab182..4961bea 100644
--- a/libultraship/src/ship/Context.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/ship/Context.cpp
@@ -392,6 +392,18 @@ std::string Context::GetShortName() {
 }
 
 std::string Context::GetAppBundlePath() {
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__)
+    // One directory, and it is known without asking. A payload is mounted at /app0 and
+    // has nothing above it and no working directory it can move, so the install, the
+    // save data and the archives are all here. `OOPS_POSIX_HOME` is the build's name for
+    // it; `common/posix/posix.c` resolves relative paths against the same place.
+    //
+    // Answering "." instead, as the fallback below does, is not wrong but is worse: it
+    // makes every path built from this one carry a `.` component through
+    // `std::filesystem`, and those reach the kernel, which does not resolve them.
+    return OOPS_POSIX_HOME;
+#endif
+
 #if defined(__ANDROID__)
     const char* externaldir = SDL_AndroidGetExternalStoragePath();
     if (externaldir != NULL) {
@@ -455,6 +467,12 @@ std::string Context::GetAppBundlePath() {
 }
 
 std::string Context::GetAppDirectoryPath(std::string appName) {
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__)
+    // The same place as the bundle, for the reason given there: there is only one.
+    (void)appName;
+    return OOPS_POSIX_HOME;
+#endif
+
 #if defined(__ANDROID__)
     const char* externaldir = SDL_AndroidGetExternalStoragePath();
     if (externaldir != NULL) {
